WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.942
Dwight Dewey Riley was born in 1971.

00:00:02.996 --> 00:00:04.142
He was the first born of Mr. Riley,

00:00:04.196 --> 00:00:05.994
 who he never meets, and

00:00:06.042 --> 00:00:08.126
Mrs. Riley, who was present in 1996.

00:00:08.228 --> 00:00:12.154
Around 1978 or 79, Dewey's younger sister Tatum was born.

00:00:12.202 --> 00:00:15.194
The Riley family lived in the Northern California town of Woodsboro.

00:00:15.242 --> 00:00:18.270
Despite it being a small town, Dewey doesn't seem to have many friends.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.363
Maybe his classmates moved on to San Francisco while he stayed back in the suburbs.

00:00:22.363 --> 00:00:26.422
As a 24 year old, Dewey watched sensational or trash news show Top Story,

00:00:26.476 --> 00:00:30.086
unaware that he would meet the host, Gale Weathers, a year later. 

00:00:30.108 --> 00:00:34.354
In September 1996, Dewey was 25 years old and in his first year as a deputy.

00:00:34.402 --> 00:00:37.638
Despite carrying a badge and gun, he was receiving very little respect at

00:00:37.644 --> 00:00:38.582
work and at home.

00:00:38.636 --> 00:00:41.866
But when a gutsy murder takes place nearby, Dewey finds that he has an

00:00:41.888 --> 00:00:44.118
opportunity to gain a little respect.

00:00:44.214 --> 00:00:47.466
The killer, soon to be infamously known as Ghostface, was cutting through

00:00:47.488 --> 00:00:48.490
his sister's high school.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.818
And though he doesn't instill a lot of faith from his peers, Deputy Dewey is

00:00:51.824 --> 00:00:55.806
going to do everything he can, even if no one else cares, because he does.

00:00:55.908 --> 00:01:00.010
To learn how and why Dewey Riley became the hero of the Scream franchise,

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:03.746
how his onscreen relationship with Gale came true in real life, and what

00:01:03.768 --> 00:01:07.506
this could mean for future Scream installments, stick around to the end of

00:01:07.528 --> 00:01:08.340
this video.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:13.074
♪ Metal Music ♪

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.026
Welcome to horror history.

00:01:15.128 --> 00:01:19.042
Of the two characters initially destined to die in the original 1996 Scream,

00:01:19.106 --> 00:01:22.914
it was deputy, then private citizen, then technical advisor, then Sheriff

00:01:22.962 --> 00:01:24.610
Dewey Riley who became the hero.

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:28.178
David Arquette, the actor, former professional wrestler and certified

00:01:28.194 --> 00:01:31.446
Boss Ross instructor, infused a lot of his actual self into the character of

00:01:31.468 --> 00:01:32.194
Dewey Riley.

00:01:32.242 --> 00:01:35.746
In an interview with Variety, he stated Dewey always had this love of

00:01:35.778 --> 00:01:38.994
Clint Eastwood and wanting to be the sort of macho, kind of tough guy, grizzled

00:01:39.042 --> 00:01:39.998
person, but he never was.

00:01:40.044 --> 00:01:42.846
Is that's how I approached the character from the start? He tried to be

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:45.210
tough and the sheriff, but he wouldn't get the respect.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:48.138
It goes back to the classic line in the first one when I wear this badge,

00:01:48.154 --> 00:01:49.630
you treat me like a man of the law.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.374
He's really not that person.

00:01:51.492 --> 00:01:54.938
The desire to be a Clint Eastwood type of character is reflected in Dewey's

00:01:54.954 --> 00:01:58.862
theme song, which was originally composed for the 1996 movie Broken Arrow.

00:01:58.926 --> 00:02:02.402
It was used in Scream Two as a temp track, but left ultimately in the final film.

00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:05.826
As with the music, Dewey's character was kept alive by a series

00:02:05.848 --> 00:02:07.582
of missteps and last minute decisions.

00:02:07.646 --> 00:02:10.914
As the franchise grew, Dewey's life was also shaped by the life of David Arquette,

00:02:10.962 --> 00:02:14.162
helping him evolve into the cowboy hero of the franchise.

00:02:14.226 --> 00:02:17.078
But to understand how he got there, we've got to take it back to the

00:02:17.084 --> 00:02:19.980
Ghostface origins in the late 90s.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.848
♪ Ominous Music ♪

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:28.486
On what would have been a quiet night in September, the Woodsboro Police Department

00:02:28.518 --> 00:02:32.218
received a 911 call that would change everything and arrive on

00:02:32.224 --> 00:02:35.482
the scene to find high school student Casey Becker gutted in a tree.

00:02:35.546 --> 00:02:38.814
Considering Casey was in the same class as Dewey's sister, this must have

00:02:38.852 --> 00:02:40.270
hit him a little closer to home.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.258
Dewey's early introduction to what would become known as the Woodsboro Murders

00:02:43.274 --> 00:02:45.819
had him taking his position as deputy very seriously.

00:02:45.819 --> 00:02:49.096
Regardless of the response from everyone

00:02:49.096 --> 00:02:53.509
– [TATUM] Dewey was saying this is the worst crime they’ve seen in years. Even worse than-

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.466
The next morning, there's a strange feeling in the air of

00:02:56.488 --> 00:02:57.474
Woodsboro High School.

00:02:57.512 --> 00:03:00.866
As the media swarm the quad, the sheriff brings Dewey along to interrogate

00:03:00.898 --> 00:03:04.134
the entire school, likely because he's the youngest member of the force and

00:03:04.172 --> 00:03:07.058
probably has familiarity with the student body because of his sister,

00:03:07.154 --> 00:03:09.110
– [SID] Officer Burke. Dewey.

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:11.590
– [DEWEY] Uh that’s Deputy Riley today, Sid.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:14.874
Right off the bat, we see that Dewey is struggling to get a girl seven years

00:03:14.912 --> 00:03:17.174
his junior to respect his title as deputy.

00:03:17.222 --> 00:03:19.990
When interviewing Sidney Prescott, he's gently, authoritative.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:23.046
It's a quality that would evolve to become both his strongest weapon and

00:03:23.088 --> 00:03:25.162
eventually, it would be part of his downfall.

00:03:25.226 --> 00:03:28.666
Another emergency call comes in later that evening after Sidney is attacked

00:03:28.698 --> 00:03:31.710
in her home and Deputy Dewey is the first responder.

00:03:32.391 --> 00:03:33.465
– [DEWEY] (screams)

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:37.258
Dewey stakes claim of catching Sidney's boyfriend Billy Loomis, who is found

00:03:37.284 --> 00:03:38.770
in Sidney's house with a cell phone.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:41.746
He isn't that surprised that it might be Billy. Evidence that he has the

00:03:41.768 --> 00:03:45.182
potential instinct to catch criminals despite his Barney Fiefdom.

00:03:45.246 --> 00:03:48.446
While Sid sits for another round of questioning conducted by Dewey, let's

00:03:48.478 --> 00:03:49.522
examine his desk.

00:03:49.586 --> 00:03:53.420
Cosmic Cop packaging taped to his computer monitor, orange plastic handcuffs,

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.266
a toy police car, and a squirt gun.

00:03:55.298 --> 00:03:58.354
It's easy to imagine that these were gag gifts from the other officers,

00:03:58.402 --> 00:04:01.750
basically mocking and hazing Dewey for being the youngest of the force.

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:05.578
But the cops do at least take him somewhat seriously, at least compared to

00:04:05.584 --> 00:04:07.174
how he's treated by his sister.

00:04:07.302 --> 00:04:08.822
– [TATUM] GodDAMN it Dewey! 

00:04:08.966 --> 00:04:12.218
– [DEWEY] What did Mom tell you? When I’m wearing this badge, you treat me like a man of the law.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:16.586
– [TATUM] I’m sorry Deputy Dewey Boy but we’re ready to go. Now. Okay?

00:04:16.586 --> 00:04:20.286
The tremble in his voice and childish need to look to a real adult to

00:04:20.308 --> 00:04:24.126
control Tatum is perhaps the best example of where Dewey stands as a man.

00:04:24.228 --> 00:04:25.382
– [DEWEY] He’s my superior!

00:04:25.466 --> 00:04:26.910
– [TATUM] The JANITOR’S your superior.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:30.718
An analysis of Dewey can't be done without also mentioning the franchise long

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:33.710
romance that developed between him and a journalist, Gale Weathers.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:36.946
The first encounter of these starcrossed lovers comes as Dewey tries to

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:39.878
sneak Tatum and Sidney out the back door of the police station to avoid the

00:04:39.884 --> 00:04:43.640
media and Gale ambushes Sidney while Dewey is busy pulling up the car.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:46.386
- [OFF-CAMERA] Nice shot.

00:04:46.578 --> 00:04:47.986
- [OFF-CAMERA] No, I need camera.

00:04:48.098 --> 00:04:51.442
Despite being a fan of Gale's show, he turns a blind eye to the assault,

00:04:51.506 --> 00:04:54.506
keeping in mind what Sidney has been through over the last year and even

00:04:54.528 --> 00:04:57.530
brings her an ice pack for her bruised hand when she sleeps over that night.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:01.774
But even with the oversight of a cop, no house with a landline is safe from Ghostface.

00:05:02.809 --> 00:05:03.629
- [SID] Hello? 

00:05:03.629 --> 00:05:05.629
– [GHOSTFACE] Hello, Sidney. 

00:05:05.629 --> 00:05:06.129
- [SID] Leave me alone!

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:11.934
Considering the effort it took to get Dewey up when he had pretty much just

00:05:11.972 --> 00:05:14.302
gone to bed, he must have been in a really deep sleep.

00:05:14.366 --> 00:05:17.010
Or maybe just having fun with the vacuum cleaner.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:22.596
- [DEWEY] Hello?

00:05:22.596 --> 00:05:24.596
 In any event, he gets there too late.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:27.906
The next morning, he breaks the news to Sidney about Billy being released on

00:05:27.928 --> 00:05:30.726
account of his phone bill being clean, and assures her that they'll find the killer.

00:05:30.748 --> 00:05:33.826
While dropping off Tatum and Sidney at school, he formally meets Gale

00:05:33.858 --> 00:05:34.870
for the first time.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:38.054
They have a flirtatious exchange, but while there is an attraction between them,

00:05:38.092 --> 00:05:41.546
Gale is clearly trying to manipulate him and compliments him on his chest.

00:05:41.568 --> 00:05:45.466
- [DEWEY] Because of my boyish good looks, muscle mass has increased my

00:05:45.488 --> 00:05:47.366
- [DEWEY] acceptance as a serious police officer.

00:05:47.478 --> 00:05:48.966
Again, this is a theme for Dewey

00:05:48.998 --> 00:05:52.106
throughout the franchise, he strives for authority not as a means of

00:05:52.128 --> 00:05:55.454
control, but as a means of respect in order to best protect the people he loves.

00:05:55.492 --> 00:05:59.322
Gale turns up the flattery, but an announcement from Principal Himbry

00:05:59.386 --> 00:06:03.182
that suspends all classes and institutes a townwide curfew interrupts her.

00:06:03.236 --> 00:06:06.258
Gale pushes a little too hard in their back and forth, allowing Dewey to

00:06:06.264 --> 00:06:08.354
pick up on her insincerity and ice her out.

00:06:08.392 --> 00:06:10.590
But the exchange still ends on a playful note.

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:16.642
- [DEWEY] If I may say so, Miss Weathers, you are much prettier in person.

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:19.862
From the beginning, Dewey saw something in Gale that no one else saw.

00:06:19.916 --> 00:06:23.158
But after the town shuts down for curfew, Dewey would make a mistake that

00:06:23.164 --> 00:06:25.560
would haunt him for the rest of his life.

00:06:25.983 --> 00:06:29.232
(IMPACT)

00:06:30.918 --> 00:06:34.175
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:38.006
While Tatum and Sidney shop for snacks, Dewey treats himself to an ice cream

00:06:38.038 --> 00:06:39.654
cone and runs into Sheriff Burke.

00:06:39.702 --> 00:06:42.918
The image of Sheriff Burke's stress smoking while Dewey licks an ice cream

00:06:42.934 --> 00:06:46.170
cone is a good visual reminder of Dewey's young naivete.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:49.178
Sheriff Burke informs Dewey that the Ghostface calls were issued by 

00:06:49.194 --> 00:06:52.362
Neil Prescott's phone, and Dewey assures him that he'll keep an eye on Sidney.

00:06:52.426 --> 00:06:55.646
Is his botched attempt to put on his sunglasses a foreshadowing of his

00:06:55.668 --> 00:06:58.166
future, missteps? Maybe not, but it's still funny.

00:06:58.218 --> 00:07:01.426
That night, he drops Sidney and Tatum off at Stu Macher's house, where the

00:07:01.448 --> 00:07:03.262
youth of America are having a party.

00:07:03.326 --> 00:07:07.246
But the eye he's supposed to be keeping on Sid is distracted when he runs

00:07:07.278 --> 00:07:08.242
into Gale Weathers again.

00:07:08.296 --> 00:07:11.470
Flustered by her presence, he foolishly allows her to join as he checks out

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:11.980
the party.

00:07:12.002 --> 00:07:14.594
Upon entering, he pretends like he's going to bust a kid for underage drinking, 

00:07:14.642 --> 00:07:17.270
only to tell him that he's kidding and to have a good time.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:20.278
Just as he wanted Tatum to respect him in the police station so he could be

00:07:20.284 --> 00:07:23.546
accepted by his fellow officers, he tries to be the cool cop so he can be

00:07:23.568 --> 00:07:25.190
liked by this group of high schoolers.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:28.170
Speaking of Tatum, she is not pleased with his guest.

00:07:28.866 --> 00:07:32.394
- [TATUM] Dewey, What is she doing here? 

00:07:32.575 --> 00:07:33.679
- [DEWEY] She's with me.

00:07:33.872 --> 00:07:37.134
He's too excited to be seen rolling with a celebrity reporter to remember

00:07:37.172 --> 00:07:39.130
the bad blood that Sidney has with Gale.

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:42.662
Tatum orders him to remove Gale before heading to the garage to get beer.

00:07:42.746 --> 00:07:46.754
Unfortunately, this interaction is also the last time that Dewey would ever

00:07:46.792 --> 00:07:48.450
see his sister alive.

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:59.026
Shortly after, he gets a report of an abandoned car up the road and uses it

00:07:59.048 --> 00:08:02.274
as an opportunity to take Gale Weathers on a little murder night stroll.

00:08:02.322 --> 00:08:04.086
She obliges and the two head off.

00:08:04.188 --> 00:08:07.558
This time, the flirtation has a little bit more sincerity, and they share a

00:08:07.564 --> 00:08:10.242
little bit about themselves while also physically getting closer.

00:08:10.306 --> 00:08:13.058
Part of the strength of Dewey and Gale's relationship was each of them

00:08:13.084 --> 00:08:15.242
willing to be vulnerable with each other so early on.

00:08:15.296 --> 00:08:18.794
He even shares his real name with her, explaining that the nickname Dewey is

00:08:18.832 --> 00:08:20.202
just something he got stuck with.

00:08:20.256 --> 00:08:22.750
- [DEWEY] It's just this town's way of not taking me serious.

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:28.382
- [GALE] What about Gale Weathers? Sounds like I'm a meteorologist or something.

00:08:28.516 --> 00:08:32.126
And speaking of Dewey's authority not being taken seriously, two cars full

00:08:32.148 --> 00:08:35.214
of teens barrel down the road en route to turning Dewey and Gale into

00:08:35.252 --> 00:08:38.626
pedestrian casualties, and he tries to somehow get the cars to freeze, which

00:08:38.648 --> 00:08:39.374
is ineffective.

00:08:39.422 --> 00:08:41.186
So he throws himself and Gale out of the way

00:08:41.208 --> 00:08:44.498
at the last second. Lying in a ditch together, Dewey and Gale gaze at each

00:08:44.504 --> 00:08:48.222
other before sharing their first kiss which he allows to go on momentarily

00:08:48.286 --> 00:08:50.962
before pulling away and telling her that he's on duty.

00:08:51.026 --> 00:08:54.198
It's a great moment of maturity for him, like earlier, when he stopped to

00:08:54.204 --> 00:08:55.954
get ice cream while keeping an eye on Sidney.

00:08:56.002 --> 00:08:59.574
He got distracted momentarily, but this time he quickly corrects course.

00:08:59.692 --> 00:09:03.782
After Gale notices the abandoned car, Dewey recognizes it as Neil Prescott's,

00:09:03.846 --> 00:09:07.574
basically concluding that Sidney's father is Ghostface and rushes with Gale

00:09:07.622 --> 00:09:08.422
back to the party.

00:09:08.486 --> 00:09:11.578
In the time they were gone, the party guests mostly cleared out, save for

00:09:11.584 --> 00:09:13.750
the important characters, and the house is quiet.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:17.435
Dewey instructs Gale to call for backup before charging in, gun drawn.

00:09:17.435 --> 00:09:18.622
As he clears each room,

00:09:18.676 --> 00:09:22.526
it's obvious he's very scared by the tremor of his gun and his fright at the

00:09:22.548 --> 00:09:24.302
screaming coming from a movie in the other room.

00:09:24.356 --> 00:09:27.906
It's a testament to his bravery, but also to his objective to protect and

00:09:27.928 --> 00:09:29.390
serve, no matter the risk.

00:09:29.470 --> 00:09:32.594
At some point, while searching the house, Stu must have snuck up on him

00:09:32.632 --> 00:09:35.686
while under the disguise of the Ghostface mask and stuck a knife into his back.

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:39.138
But even that doesn't stop him from trying to respond to Sidney's

00:09:39.154 --> 00:09:40.038
screams for help.

00:09:40.124 --> 00:09:41.480
Keyword... trying.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:43.885
- [SID] Dewey!

00:09:43.885 --> 00:09:47.662
And that was the end of Deputy Dwight Dewey Riley or it would have

00:09:47.662 --> 00:09:50.354
been if David Arquette hadn't been so good in the role.

00:09:50.402 --> 00:09:53.786
As original writer Kevin Williamson recounted during the course of the

00:09:53.808 --> 00:09:56.454
movie, we realized how his performance was just so witty.

00:09:56.502 --> 00:09:59.562
He played it with such heart, such commitment, and everyone kept thinking

00:09:59.616 --> 00:10:02.778
that about halfway through it, they were asking me about a sequel, because I

00:10:02.784 --> 00:10:04.038
had already written the outline.

00:10:04.134 --> 00:10:07.214
They were like, what about the sequel? Why isn't Dewey in the sequel?

00:10:07.252 --> 00:10:11.011
And so, just in case, we filmed that last sequence of him getting in the ambulance.

00:10:11.011 --> 00:10:13.706
The decision to keep Dewey alive would become the major shaping

00:10:13.738 --> 00:10:17.106
force on the entire Scream franchise and link the fictional events to our

00:10:17.128 --> 00:10:19.166
real world through the actor David Arquette.

00:10:19.198 --> 00:10:21.202
And it starts with what happened next.

00:10:21.336 --> 00:10:24.306
Shortly after regaining consciousness, Dewey would have found out about his

00:10:24.328 --> 00:10:27.458
sister's death, and I'd imagine that his failure to protect her could be

00:10:27.464 --> 00:10:30.014
part of the reason that he decided to leave the Woodsboro police force

00:10:30.062 --> 00:10:33.622
shortly after, along with his injuries. Due to the nerve damage on his back,

00:10:33.676 --> 00:10:34.802
he would develop a limp.

00:10:34.866 --> 00:10:38.950
But letting go of the badge does not mean letting go of his desire to protect.

00:10:39.078 --> 00:10:41.958
But those who needed protection didn't stick around for long.

00:10:42.044 --> 00:10:46.149
Sidney and Randy would seemingly graduate early and head off to Windsor College in Ohio.

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:48.026
Gale would take off back to New York.

00:10:48.128 --> 00:10:50.262
After all, they did just meet two days prior. Barely.

00:10:50.326 --> 00:10:53.626
There, she would finish up her book, The Woodsboro Murders, which

00:10:53.648 --> 00:10:56.926
Dewey was excited to read, only to find that she had portrayed him as a

00:10:56.948 --> 00:10:57.850
complete idiot.

00:10:57.930 --> 00:11:01.294
The book was adapted into a movie, Stab, which Dewey doesn't show that much

00:11:01.332 --> 00:11:04.746
interest in, despite being portrayed by David Schwimmer from Friends. 

00:11:04.778 --> 00:11:07.906
That's honestly understandable it's a movie about the worst moments of his life.

00:11:08.008 --> 00:11:11.026
Seeing it alone with none of the other people involved wouldn't have been

00:11:11.048 --> 00:11:11.548
much fun.

00:11:11.576 --> 00:11:14.142
But the movie actually creates an opportunity for a reunion.

00:11:14.206 --> 00:11:18.622
On April 13, 1997, Dewey sees a report from Windsor College in Ohio

00:11:18.686 --> 00:11:22.473
regarding the murder of two students the night before at an early screening of Stab.

00:11:22.546 --> 00:11:25.986
So he got on the first flight he could find, where a year ago, we'd rarely

00:11:26.018 --> 00:11:27.186
seen him out of uniform.

00:11:27.298 --> 00:11:31.110
This Dewey is in a baggy jacket, holding his right arm awkwardly at his side

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:32.114
with a heavy limp.

00:11:32.162 --> 00:11:35.066
Judging from their reunion, Sidney and Dewey haven't seen each other in a

00:11:35.088 --> 00:11:38.746
while. And later, Randy asks about Dewey's limp and arm, indicating that he

00:11:38.768 --> 00:11:41.030
hadn't been in touch since The Woodsboro murders.

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:44.682
There may be an explanation for this, since Scream takes place in September

00:11:44.746 --> 00:11:48.158
1996, as evidenced by these calendars, among other things.

00:11:48.244 --> 00:11:51.998
And Scream Two takes place in April 1997, which is clearly shown on the

00:11:52.004 --> 00:11:53.034
movie theater marquee.

00:11:53.082 --> 00:11:56.702
We can assume that Sidney and Randy didn't make it to the end of the 96/97

00:11:56.756 --> 00:12:00.366
high school year and instead were allowed to graduate early and go directly

00:12:00.398 --> 00:12:02.462
to college, where they could begin on a winter term.

00:12:02.526 --> 00:12:05.554
A change of scenery would be healthy for them, even if it means not having

00:12:05.592 --> 00:12:06.990
time to say goodbye to Dewey.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:10.738
Their reunion, however, could certainly have occurred under happier

00:12:10.834 --> 00:12:11.990
circumstances.

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:15.437
(IMPACT)

00:12:16.901 --> 00:12:20.180
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:12:20.705 --> 00:12:23.846
When Dewey finds Sidney at her college campus, he doesn't share what he's

00:12:23.878 --> 00:12:26.838
specifically been doing for the last year, but it's safe to assume that it's

00:12:26.854 --> 00:12:27.914
been a lonely one.

00:12:28.032 --> 00:12:29.210
- [DEWEY] I was just worried.

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:34.458
- [DEWEY] Look, Sid, if there is some freaked out psycho trying to follow on Billy Loomis's

00:12:34.474 --> 00:12:37.120
- [DEWEY] footsteps, you probably already know him.

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:39.120
- [DEWEY] Or her.

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:40.718
- [DEWEY] Or them.

00:12:40.804 --> 00:12:43.994
He's completely right and even tries to make her aware to be on the lookout

00:12:44.042 --> 00:12:47.246
for a white male, which is statistically the most probable for a serial killer. 

00:12:47.278 --> 00:12:49.918
Wait a minute.

00:12:50.094 --> 00:12:53.326
Dewey implores Sidney to be careful and assures her that he'll be hanging

00:12:53.358 --> 00:12:54.418
around just in case.

00:12:54.504 --> 00:12:56.962
I always took his involvement to be kind of a cope for him.

00:12:57.016 --> 00:12:59.974
He wasn't able to save Tatum, so he's going to try to make up for it by

00:13:00.012 --> 00:13:01.078
saving her best friend.

00:13:01.164 --> 00:13:02.694
Sidney has a similar take.

00:13:02.812 --> 00:13:04.611
- [RANDY] Deputy Dewey. Woodsboro's finest.

00:13:04.658 --> 00:13:06.500
- [RANDY] What's he doing here?

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:08.082
-[SID] He's worried our surrogate big brother.

00:13:08.226 --> 00:13:11.086
It wouldn't be the last time he tried to cope using a surrogate.

00:13:11.138 --> 00:13:13.894
It was his care for Sidney, though, that brought him out to the Midwest.

00:13:13.942 --> 00:13:16.810
But he'd also run into someone he didn't care to see.

00:13:16.946 --> 00:13:23.470
- [DEWEY] Page 32. Deputy Dewey filled the room with his Barney Fife-ish presence.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:25.600
- [GALE] You read my book?

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:27.354
- [DEWEY] Yes, I do read, Miss Weathers.

00:13:27.402 --> 00:13:31.166
- [GALE] Oh, Dewey, don't take it so seriously. It's a character in a book.

00:13:31.316 --> 00:13:37.482
- [DEWEY] Page 41. Deputy Dewey oozed with inexperience.

00:13:37.626 --> 00:13:41.186
To be fair, Dewey did literally the opposite of what he was told to do by

00:13:41.208 --> 00:13:42.286
the sheriff in Woodsboro.

00:13:42.318 --> 00:13:45.218
He left Sidney and Tatum at the party and walked off with Gale down the road. 

00:13:45.224 --> 00:13:46.446
It's all part of the ride.

00:13:46.478 --> 00:13:47.778
But Gale had a point.

00:13:47.864 --> 00:13:50.770
However, he feels justified in calling her money hungry and heartless.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:53.718
On the other hand, he's probably the only one who can speak to Gale like

00:13:53.724 --> 00:13:55.250
that without her going nuclear.

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:58.694
- [DEWEY] How do you know that my dim witted inexperience isn't merely a subtle form

00:13:58.732 --> 00:14:07.757
- [DEWEY]  of manipulation used to lower people's expectations, thereby enhancing my ability to effectively maneuver within any given situation? 

00:14:07.788 --> 00:14:09.110
Because your sister wouldn't be dead.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:13.134
Dewey is harboring a lot of pain over his characterization in Gale's book.

00:14:13.172 --> 00:14:16.366
And who can blame it? The year before, he vented to Gale about how he was

00:14:16.388 --> 00:14:19.114
just trying to get people to call him Dwight, or at least deputy.

00:14:19.162 --> 00:14:22.526
And what does she do to the man who risked his life for her? She sees to it

00:14:22.548 --> 00:14:25.646
that the whole world disrespects him by portraying him as a doofus in her

00:14:25.668 --> 00:14:26.738
widely published book.

00:14:26.824 --> 00:14:28.610
Talk about kicking a cripple when he's down.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.906
And despite all of that, he still can't help himself from complimenting her hair.

00:14:31.928 --> 00:14:33.646
- [DEWEY] Nice streaks.

00:14:33.758 --> 00:14:34.290
That night.

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:37.794
Student CiCi Cooper is stabbed and thrown from the top of her sorority house

00:14:37.832 --> 00:14:40.069
and Ghostface goes after Sidney shortly after.

00:14:40.069 --> 00:14:41.122
Dewey gives chase.

00:14:41.186 --> 00:14:44.898
But with his limp, Ghostface slips away after leaving a slice in Derek's arm

00:14:44.914 --> 00:14:45.782
to remember him by.

00:14:45.836 --> 00:14:48.934
Dewey grows suspicious of Derek's near miss and can't help but play

00:14:48.972 --> 00:14:50.786
detective when speaking to Windsor's Police Chief.

00:14:50.818 --> 00:14:54.314
- [DEWEY] Do you think someone's trying to duplicate Woodsboro?

00:14:54.352 --> 00:14:54.816
- [GALE] It looks like it.

00:14:54.816 --> 00:14:56.878
- [DEWEY] Think you have a copycat on your hands, Chief? 

00:14:56.878 --> 00:15:01.562
So Dewey does some of his own investigating. With Woodsboro survivor film expert and Windsor College

00:15:01.616 --> 00:15:03.046
film student Randy Meeks.

00:15:03.158 --> 00:15:06.782
The two run through possible suspects, including Derek and themselves.

00:15:06.916 --> 00:15:09.690
Yet, Dewey balks at the idea of Gale being a suspect.

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:12.766
He enjoys cutting her down a little, but in the end, he's more willing to

00:15:12.788 --> 00:15:16.102
make himself a suspect than assume that Gale is a Ghostface killer.

00:15:16.186 --> 00:15:18.894
- [DEWEY] No, Gale's a lot of things, but Gale's not a killer.

00:15:18.942 --> 00:15:21.970
Later on the quad, they continue sharing theories which all amount to

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:25.662
incredulously, accepting that these are Woodsboro copycat killings.

00:15:25.726 --> 00:15:29.186
The first mention of Tatum by name causes Dewey to wince, confirming that

00:15:29.208 --> 00:15:31.478
there's grief and possibly guilt still there.

00:15:31.564 --> 00:15:34.886
Before he has time to process that, Gale gets an incoming Ghost face call of

00:15:34.908 --> 00:15:36.502
her own, and Randy picks it up.

00:15:36.556 --> 00:15:40.006
Seeing an opportunity, Gale and Dewey partner off, leaving Randy to keep

00:15:40.028 --> 00:15:42.346
Ghostface on the line while they try to search for him.

00:15:42.368 --> 00:15:45.802
After assaulting several strangers, it dawns on them that they have no idea

00:15:45.856 --> 00:15:48.054
where Randy is while being pursued by a killer

00:15:48.102 --> 00:15:52.202
and Randy becomes the next victim under Dewey's watch, just like Tatum

00:15:52.256 --> 00:15:52.998
seven months prior.

00:15:53.094 --> 00:15:56.810
That would not be the only similarity to 1996 Cotton Weary.

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:59.162
The number one suspect at the time is released.

00:15:59.226 --> 00:16:02.362
Much like Billy Loomis, the campus is given an evening curfew.

00:16:02.426 --> 00:16:05.422
Dewey swears, Cotton or not, that he'll find the guy responsible.

00:16:05.486 --> 00:16:08.866
And just when it feels like the story might unfold just as it did before,

00:16:08.968 --> 00:16:10.718
Gale adds a shocking twist.

00:16:10.814 --> 00:16:13.102
She takes responsibility for herself.

00:16:13.246 --> 00:16:14.850
- [GALE] I feel bad, Dewey.

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:18.550
- [GALE] I feel really bad.

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:23.597
- [GALE]  I never say that because I never feel bad about anything, but I feel bad now.

00:16:23.597 --> 00:16:24.694
This is huge.

00:16:24.812 --> 00:16:28.518
Without Gale's sincerity, the two can't fully establish the trust needed to

00:16:28.524 --> 00:16:30.290
get them through the next couple installments.

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:33.174
At first, Dewey is mistrustful thinking that she's performing.

00:16:33.222 --> 00:16:36.186
But in the end, they come together out of their mutual desire to bring the

00:16:36.208 --> 00:16:37.286
culprit to justice.

00:16:37.398 --> 00:16:40.522
It is perhaps their most important scene together because from here on out,

00:16:40.576 --> 00:16:42.982
Dewey and Gale became fully intertwined in the series.

00:16:43.046 --> 00:16:45.866
Their teamwork quickly pays off when they realize that Gale has crowd

00:16:45.898 --> 00:16:48.766
footage shot for her story, which they realize might be an excellent place

00:16:48.788 --> 00:16:49.962
to start looking for the killer.

00:16:50.026 --> 00:16:53.846
A VHS viewing session in the film's lecture hall leads to Gale apologizing

00:16:53.898 --> 00:16:56.734
for hurting Dewey's feelings, which leads to an impromptu tryst.

00:16:56.782 --> 00:16:59.822
And like their moment together before finding Neil Prescott's car, 

00:16:59.886 --> 00:17:01.246
Gale comes to a realization.

00:17:01.438 --> 00:17:04.530
- [GALE] Dewey, that's not my footage.

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:07.982
Someone is playing this additional footage on a second TV.

00:17:08.046 --> 00:17:11.666
And inevitably, Dewey and Gale find themselves in an old fashioned Ghostface pursuit.

00:17:11.698 --> 00:17:16.029
They end up separated, with Gale accidentally trapping herself in a recording studio.

00:17:16.082 --> 00:17:18.946
With only one exit, she successfully dodges Ghostface.

00:17:18.978 --> 00:17:22.646
Slipping into the soundproof side of the studio, Dewey unfortunately enters

00:17:22.678 --> 00:17:25.130
on the other side, unaware that Ghostface is in the room.

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:28.666
Just as he peers through the window searching for Gale, Ghostface jams the

00:17:28.688 --> 00:17:31.898
knife into Dewey's back with the last of his strength, the Dewey finds the

00:17:31.904 --> 00:17:35.034
mic to yell out a warning to Gale before he is dispatched on the glass

00:17:35.082 --> 00:17:35.742
beside her.

00:17:35.796 --> 00:17:39.166
It seemed the events of Woodsboro past really were repeating themselves,

00:17:39.268 --> 00:17:42.366
because once again, Dewey would find himself out of commission for the finale. 

00:17:42.388 --> 00:17:46.490
But luckily, once again, he leaves the next morning in an ambulance,

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:47.574
not a body bag.

00:17:47.642 --> 00:17:50.926
We see how far Dewey and Gale's relationship has come when she immediately

00:17:50.958 --> 00:17:52.834
drops her news microphone at the sight of him.

00:17:52.872 --> 00:17:56.452
Unlike their previous adventure, where she was more concerned with getting the shot. 

00:17:56.452 --> 00:18:01.194
According to this first responder, it was actually Dewey's traumatic past that saved his life.

00:18:01.194 --> 00:18:03.770
- [FIRST RESPONDER] Knife went into some old scar tissue, saved his life. 

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:06.598
After realizing how much they cared about each other, the two would try to

00:18:06.604 --> 00:18:10.323
make it work by living in Woodsboro, where Gale took care of him until he was well.

00:18:10.332 --> 00:18:13.546
But Gale Weathers has never been a small town character, and she never

00:18:13.568 --> 00:18:15.210
misses an opportunity to say this.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:18.346
While Dewey can't seem to go anywhere without bringing Woodsboro with him.

00:18:18.368 --> 00:18:21.418
If one of them wasn't willing to relocate, then it was never going to

00:18:21.424 --> 00:18:22.982
work romantically in the long term.

00:18:23.046 --> 00:18:26.798
After a year, Gale left to chase an opportunity on 60 Minutes 2.

00:18:26.884 --> 00:18:30.478
Ironically, being the only core legacy character to consistently return to

00:18:30.484 --> 00:18:33.406
Woodsboro probably made it easy for the Stab Three production team to

00:18:33.428 --> 00:18:33.928
find him.

00:18:33.956 --> 00:18:38.034
Sometime after Gale leaves, Dewey accepts an out of town job himself in

00:18:38.072 --> 00:18:40.370
Hollywood, or at least Studio City.

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:43.822
Due to his firsthand experience, he comes onto Stab Three as a technical advisor.

00:18:43.886 --> 00:18:47.586
This is kind of a 180 for him, considering he showed no interest in

00:18:47.608 --> 00:18:50.854
the Stab franchise before this, but he was probably lonely after things

00:18:50.892 --> 00:18:53.074
didn't work with Gale and the cast of this movie.

00:18:53.122 --> 00:18:55.974
Pretending to be his friends were the closest he could have to actually

00:18:56.012 --> 00:18:57.206
having those friends together.

00:18:57.308 --> 00:19:00.474
Inevitably, they were not the only remnants of his past to be found on this production.

00:19:00.512 --> 00:19:05.434
The Return of Ghostface would wreck havoc on more than just the shooting sketches.

00:19:05.676 --> 00:19:07.596
(IMPACT)

00:19:10.299 --> 00:19:14.050
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:19:14.050 --> 00:19:18.458
In July 1999, Dewey serves as a technical advisor on a recreated set version

00:19:18.474 --> 00:19:21.962
of Woodsboro, frozen at each brutal murder, including his sisters.

00:19:22.026 --> 00:19:24.602
Surely that can't be helpful for his grief processing.

00:19:24.666 --> 00:19:27.794
Despite this, it's not hard to figure out why the job is attractive for him.

00:19:27.832 --> 00:19:31.294
He has a little authority on set, plus he works most closely with actress

00:19:31.342 --> 00:19:34.222
Jennifer Jolie, who happens to be playing Gale Weathers.

00:19:34.286 --> 00:19:37.374
Just as Sidney had become sort of a surrogate sister for him during Scream Two,

00:19:37.422 --> 00:19:40.646
Jennifer is his surrogate girlfriend though I'm pretty sure it's more

00:19:40.668 --> 00:19:42.534
of an emotional surrogate than a physical one.

00:19:42.572 --> 00:19:45.798
With Jennifer referring to Dewey as her rock, he ends up moving into a

00:19:45.804 --> 00:19:48.070
trailer on her property, which, if you know, LA

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:51.542
and housing costs, is probably the nicest thing anyone's ever done for him.

00:19:51.596 --> 00:19:54.714
Sidney has moved into a life of seclusion, with her whereabouts hidden from

00:19:54.752 --> 00:19:58.218
everyone except Dewey, who seems to be his most focused when he knows that

00:19:58.224 --> 00:19:58.918
she's safe.

00:19:59.014 --> 00:20:01.910
Dewey isn't the only former Woodsboro resident on staff.

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:05.114
Cotton Weary is set to make a cameo in the movie as himself.

00:20:05.242 --> 00:20:08.922
That is, until he becomes the victim of yet another Ghostface killer.

00:20:08.986 --> 00:20:09.742
This prompts

00:20:09.796 --> 00:20:13.086
LA Detective Mark Kincaid to hire the real Gale Weathers, seeing as how she

00:20:13.108 --> 00:20:16.434
literally wrote the book on Ghostface, placing her directly in the path of

00:20:16.472 --> 00:20:17.342
Dewey Riley.

00:20:17.406 --> 00:20:21.554
- [DEWEY] Well, surprise, surprise, someone dies and Gale comes running.

00:20:21.752 --> 00:20:25.714
This is a confident, maybe even happier, Dewey than the morose, broken man

00:20:25.752 --> 00:20:27.858
who showed up on campus in 1997.

00:20:27.944 --> 00:20:30.806
I'm not suggesting that living on a movie star's driveway because she

00:20:30.828 --> 00:20:33.926
reminds him of someone he loves is the ultimate dream for him, but I think

00:20:33.948 --> 00:20:37.334
his slightly improved state is probably tied to our main through line in this video.

00:20:37.372 --> 00:20:40.694
After surviving two Ghostface attacks, Dewey has gained a little respect.

00:20:40.732 --> 00:20:43.178
The actors see him as the real thing.

00:20:43.264 --> 00:20:45.930
Dewey grins at his Tom Prince casting and Stab Three.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:49.514
Despite Gale's incredulous laugh, that alone is proof that he no longer

00:20:49.552 --> 00:20:51.018
needs to hang on her every word.

00:20:51.104 --> 00:20:54.502
That night, Ghostface stabs again, taking out another cast member.

00:20:54.566 --> 00:20:57.866
The next day, Dewey and Gale sit down to lunch, and Dewey looks perturbed

00:20:57.898 --> 00:21:00.926
when she reveals that the police approached her to help investigate the new murders. 

00:21:00.948 --> 00:21:04.346
Sure, Gale wrote the definitive book on the Woodsboro murders,

00:21:04.378 --> 00:21:05.966
but Dewey was actually a cop.

00:21:06.068 --> 00:21:09.314
There are reasons why they might approach Gale over Dewey, like the fact

00:21:09.352 --> 00:21:13.154
that Dewey is a part of the production and probably a suspect, but from his

00:21:13.192 --> 00:21:16.658
point of view, he just got overlooked for the person he almost died for.

00:21:16.744 --> 00:21:18.546
- [GALE] You said you'd never leave Woodsboro.

00:21:18.658 --> 00:21:20.280
- [GALE] It's the only place that's real.

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:24.358
- [GALE] But now you're here, not with me.

00:21:24.444 --> 00:21:28.006
It's clear that Gale did want Dewey to come with her, but in his mind, she

00:21:28.028 --> 00:21:31.154
wanted to be someone else and didn't try to make it work in Woodsboro.

00:21:31.202 --> 00:21:34.394
He's deflecting from the reality that it was Dewey who never tried to meet

00:21:34.432 --> 00:21:36.058
her halfway in their romantic life.

00:21:36.144 --> 00:21:38.730
When it comes to catching Ghostface, however, he's all in.

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:39.322
Off the record.

00:21:39.376 --> 00:21:42.922
He fills Gale in on the information he has, but he's interrupted by a page

00:21:42.976 --> 00:21:43.994
from Jennifer Jolie.

00:21:44.042 --> 00:21:47.082
He gives Gale the same line he gave her after their first kiss.

00:21:47.226 --> 00:21:49.974
- [GALE] Wait, Dewey, where are you going?
- [DEWEY] I'm on duty. 

00:21:49.974 --> 00:21:51.242
A distraught Jennifer catches Dewey up on

00:21:51.393 --> 00:21:54.602
the second victim, Sarah Darling, and the pattern is revealed.

00:21:54.666 --> 00:21:57.774
Each victim has been taken out in the same order as the deaths in the

00:21:57.822 --> 00:22:01.182
Stab Three script, and next up is Gale, which means trouble for Jennifer.

00:22:01.246 --> 00:22:04.526
Dewey tries to take control of the situation using the authority and respect

00:22:04.558 --> 00:22:06.814
he's fostered as a former law enforcement hero.

00:22:06.862 --> 00:22:09.922
However, not everyone sees him the same way he sees himself.

00:22:10.066 --> 00:22:12.874
-[STEPHEN STONE] Hey, do drop have a word?

00:22:12.874 --> 00:22:15.426
Jennifer's bodyguard, Stephen Stone, still speaks

00:22:15.458 --> 00:22:18.966
down to him and reminds him who the professional celebrity guard is and who

00:22:18.988 --> 00:22:21.930
the failed cop whose resume reads like an obituary is.

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:25.146
Ouch. I absolutely love the nickname Dew Drop, though.

00:22:25.248 --> 00:22:28.698
With Stone taking care of Jennifer, Dewey joins Detective Kincaid and the

00:22:28.704 --> 00:22:31.786
LAPD down at the Stab Three production office, where he's reminded that

00:22:31.808 --> 00:22:34.678
there were three versions of the script, thus three different people that

00:22:34.704 --> 00:22:35.486
could die next.

00:22:35.588 --> 00:22:38.426
Due to all the unknowns, production on Stab Three is canceled.

00:22:38.458 --> 00:22:41.866
So the remaining cast members all meet back at Jennifer Jolie's for a gloomy

00:22:41.898 --> 00:22:43.966
rap party, if you want to call it that.

00:22:44.068 --> 00:22:47.338
Turns out, gathering all the possible victims in one house wasn't the

00:22:47.364 --> 00:22:48.050
perfect idea.

00:22:48.120 --> 00:22:49.906
And this leads to a Ghostface attack.

00:22:50.008 --> 00:22:52.174
Stephen Stone gets a knife in Dewey's trailer.

00:22:52.222 --> 00:22:55.586
Who's the dew drop now? He manages to stagger out to the front door, where he

00:22:55.608 --> 00:22:58.670
collapses in front of everybody, sending the whole cast into a panic.

00:22:58.750 --> 00:23:01.842
Suddenly, new script pages start coming in on Jennifer's fax machine.

00:23:01.906 --> 00:23:04.758
Dewey realizes it's a trap and orders everyone to go outside.

00:23:04.844 --> 00:23:08.394
But his Hollywood counterpart, Tom Prince, lets his curiosity get the better

00:23:08.432 --> 00:23:11.210
of him, which ends up being a fatal mistake.

00:23:15.070 --> 00:23:19.082
The blast propels Dewey, Jennifer, and Gale downhill splitting the party up.

00:23:19.136 --> 00:23:22.186
He finds himself in a real Sophie's Choice, with Jennifer calling for him

00:23:22.208 --> 00:23:24.090
from one direction and Gale from the other.

00:23:24.160 --> 00:23:27.626
He doesn't hesitate before marching towards Gale, the real Gale, and reaches

00:23:27.658 --> 00:23:30.938
her just in time to fire off a shot and save her from Ghost fans.

00:23:31.114 --> 00:23:32.560
- [GALE] Thanks for saving me.

00:23:33.010 --> 00:23:34.400
- [DEWEY] It's habit.

00:23:35.650 --> 00:23:39.166
The next day, Sidney finally arrives in Los Angeles, hoping to help solve

00:23:39.198 --> 00:23:39.698
the mystery.

00:23:39.742 --> 00:23:43.006
And shortly after, they receive a video containing the rules of surviving

00:23:43.038 --> 00:23:46.526
the rare horror trilogy by none other than the deceased Randy Meeks.

00:23:46.638 --> 00:23:49.894
Unlike when Randy tried to deliver the rules to him at Windsor College two

00:23:49.932 --> 00:23:53.426
years prior and Dewey interrupted him to get to the point, this time he's

00:23:53.458 --> 00:23:54.210
taking notes.

00:23:54.290 --> 00:23:57.606
This really emphasizes Dewey's growing belief in the rules and thus his

00:23:57.628 --> 00:23:58.662
willingness to learn them.

00:23:58.716 --> 00:24:01.594
He's not just randomly searching for a killer, he's learning how they operate.

00:24:01.632 --> 00:24:04.982
With a more focused direction provided by Randy. RIP.

00:24:05.046 --> 00:24:07.258
Gale unsurprisingly splits off.

00:24:07.424 --> 00:24:09.958
Do you want us to come with you? I work better alone.

00:24:10.054 --> 00:24:11.990
No. History says you really don't.

00:24:12.070 --> 00:24:15.458
Meanwhile, Dewey is doing his own investigating on set when he hears Sidney

00:24:15.494 --> 00:24:16.222
calling for him.

00:24:16.276 --> 00:24:18.974
He fights through his nerve damage to reach her as fast as he can.

00:24:19.012 --> 00:24:21.710
But the second Dewey hobbles in Ghostface runs off.

00:24:21.780 --> 00:24:24.606
The whole thing is a parallel of Billy's first attack on Sid and

00:24:24.628 --> 00:24:27.358
Dewey is the first responder on the scene in both instances.

00:24:27.454 --> 00:24:30.546
Once Sidney is settled at the precinct and following a confrontation with

00:24:30.568 --> 00:24:34.178
Stab's producer about Maureen Prescott's past in Hollywood, Dewey, Gale and

00:24:34.184 --> 00:24:37.454
Jennifer head off to the birthday party of Roman, the director of Stab Three,

00:24:37.502 --> 00:24:40.290
and totally not Ghostface or Sidney's half brother.

00:24:40.370 --> 00:24:43.270
The party splits up again because they just never learn.

00:24:43.340 --> 00:24:46.166
But Dewey and Gale stay back to wait for Sidney to arrive, where they

00:24:46.188 --> 00:24:49.122
discover Ghostface mask, cell phone and voice changer.

00:24:49.186 --> 00:24:52.294
Then they split up because they just never learn.

00:24:52.412 --> 00:24:55.866
Gale and Jennifer only manage to find him moments before he gets popped by

00:24:55.888 --> 00:24:59.066
Ghostface, who slices him on the arm and knocks him out of commission just

00:24:59.088 --> 00:25:01.878
long enough to take two more victims from the Stab Three cast.

00:25:01.974 --> 00:25:05.722
As he comes to and examines his injuries, Gale brings him his gun or

00:25:05.776 --> 00:25:06.346
someone's gun.

00:25:06.378 --> 00:25:07.742
I've kind of lost track at this point.

00:25:07.796 --> 00:25:09.438
And he sees the bedroom mirror moving.

00:25:09.524 --> 00:25:12.046
He risks the seven years of bad luck by shooting through it.

00:25:12.068 --> 00:25:15.662
And Jennifer comes crashing through the glass shards, or should I say

00:25:15.796 --> 00:25:16.990
Jennifer's body.

00:25:17.140 --> 00:25:21.182
Dewey is mortified to lose the cast member he connected most with, and Gale

00:25:21.246 --> 00:25:24.498
is even more mortified to see the grim image of someone who is supposed to

00:25:24.504 --> 00:25:25.586
be portraying her.

00:25:25.688 --> 00:25:29.198
So they do the most logical thing anyone would do in this scenario.

00:25:29.294 --> 00:25:29.810
Not really.

00:25:29.880 --> 00:25:30.790
They split up again.

00:25:30.860 --> 00:25:33.430
When he realizes he can't find her, he freaks out.

00:25:33.500 --> 00:25:36.454
Gale calls his phone and tells him that she's trapped in the basement, but

00:25:36.492 --> 00:25:39.686
because of the voice changer, he second guesses this, suspicious that it may

00:25:39.708 --> 00:25:41.590
be the killer trying to lure him down there.

00:25:41.660 --> 00:25:45.206
However, when he hears her scream movie title, he opens the basement door

00:25:45.238 --> 00:25:48.118
anyway and Ghostface knocks him out with the dull end of a knife.

00:25:48.214 --> 00:25:51.754
As a result, Dewey and Gale are captured by Ghostface, but luckily for them,

00:25:51.792 --> 00:25:55.002
he keeps them alive to use as base to lure in his main target, Sidney.

00:25:55.066 --> 00:25:59.034
And Dew Drop can only watch as Ghostface chases her into the secret

00:25:59.082 --> 00:26:01.898
screening room, where all would be revealed.

00:26:01.994 --> 00:26:05.006
It was Roman who is also Sidney's half brother.

00:26:05.118 --> 00:26:06.450
Sorry I lied.

00:26:06.692 --> 00:26:10.364
(IMPACT)

00:26:11.512 --> 00:26:15.062
♪ Metal Music ♪

00:26:15.270 --> 00:26:18.706
After breaking free from the chair he is bound in, Dewey frees Gale and

00:26:18.728 --> 00:26:22.271
retrieves the gun from Detective Kincaid, who has also been injured by Roman.

00:26:22.271 --> 00:26:24.370
Dewey ends up being the last cop standing.

00:26:24.450 --> 00:26:27.206
Perhaps this gave him the confidence to return to the police force in the future.

00:26:27.228 --> 00:26:30.264
Or perhaps it was the heroics that would soon follow. 

00:26:30.264 --> 00:26:35.546
After barging into the library and sticking a pair of tweezers in the outlet to turn off

00:26:35.568 --> 00:26:36.346
the power.

00:26:36.528 --> 00:26:37.770
Don't try that at home.

00:26:37.840 --> 00:26:40.938
He's able to navigate the secret corridors of the mansion and ram down the

00:26:40.944 --> 00:26:44.438
screening room door right after the conclusion of Sid's battle with Roman.

00:26:44.534 --> 00:26:47.706
This time he demonstrates that he really was paying attention during Randy's

00:26:47.738 --> 00:26:50.954
tape because he's the one to remind the others of the horror movie rules,

00:26:51.002 --> 00:26:54.190
this time about the killer being superhuman at the end of a trilogy.

00:26:54.270 --> 00:26:56.580
As usual, Randy was spot off

00:27:05.510 --> 00:27:07.046
- [SID] Dewey. 
- [DEWY] What? 

00:27:07.046 --> 00:27:08.754
- [SID]Head. Shoot him in the head.

00:27:08.872 --> 00:27:10.302
Third time's a charm, I guess.

00:27:10.376 --> 00:27:13.606
This time Dewey stays in the game long enough and finally gets to be the hero.

00:27:13.628 --> 00:27:17.346
Sometime later, the group returns to Sidney's remote home in the hills

00:27:17.378 --> 00:27:19.106
to help her settle back in, I suppose.

00:27:19.218 --> 00:27:23.030
Knowing that this adventure is over, and with Roman gone, possibly for good,

00:27:23.100 --> 00:27:26.474
he probably realizes that his time with Gale will be coming to a close soon.

00:27:26.512 --> 00:27:29.878
If he doesn't make a move, he asks her to sign his copy of The Woodsboro Murders,

00:27:29.894 --> 00:27:33.594
 only when she opens it up, she finds an Andy Dufresne style proposal. 

00:27:33.642 --> 00:27:37.280
- [DEWEY] I know it'll never work.

00:27:38.050 --> 00:27:45.281
- [DEWEY] You know it'll never work but what I'm asking you just to see if we're wrong.

00:27:45.281 --> 00:27:46.526
They weren't wrong.

00:27:46.708 --> 00:27:47.978
What? They weren't.

00:27:48.074 --> 00:27:51.826
However, the two did go on to get married in 2001, and things would go well

00:27:51.848 --> 00:27:52.402
for a while.

00:27:52.456 --> 00:27:54.914
With the superstar limo of Scream sequels behind them.

00:27:54.952 --> 00:27:58.142
The new millennium was much quieter and more peaceful for Dewey and Gale.

00:27:58.206 --> 00:28:01.126
They settled down together in Woodsboro, with Gale finally giving a

00:28:01.148 --> 00:28:03.174
chance to that dreaded small town life.

00:28:03.292 --> 00:28:06.982
As I alluded to earlier, Dewey became a cop again, and this time he quickly

00:28:07.036 --> 00:28:09.610
rose up through the ranks due to his extensive experience.

00:28:09.760 --> 00:28:14.006
As years went by without a new ghost face, his younger reputation of Deputy

00:28:14.038 --> 00:28:17.094
Dewey boy and Do Drop slowly faded to memory.

00:28:17.222 --> 00:28:20.506
Eventually, he became Woodsboro's sheriff, finally achieving the

00:28:20.528 --> 00:28:23.258
strongest symbol of respect he had long sought after.

00:28:23.344 --> 00:28:26.622
Dewey maintains his care and protectiveness over his loved ones, though

00:28:26.676 --> 00:28:28.634
Sidney is, of course, not in Woodsboro.

00:28:28.682 --> 00:28:31.898
Regardless, he holds on to his surrogate brother role and reads Sidney's

00:28:31.914 --> 00:28:34.430
book, Out of Darkness, cover to cover when it comes out.

00:28:34.500 --> 00:28:37.762
As the added responsibilities of his job begin to require more of him,

00:28:37.816 --> 00:28:40.946
cracks start to show in his relationship with Gale, who is having a hard

00:28:40.968 --> 00:28:44.386
time finding her purpose after moving from nonfiction to fiction and

00:28:44.408 --> 00:28:47.314
suffering from writer's block, which is made worse by the lack of a friend

00:28:47.352 --> 00:28:48.500
network in the area.

00:28:48.500 --> 00:28:52.950
In September 2011, and I'm basing that date on this line from Scream 2022.

00:28:53.020 --> 00:28:55.014
Sheriff Riley wakes up and goes on his way.

00:28:55.052 --> 00:28:57.926
But the morning begins with a haunting similarity to the night of the

00:28:57.948 --> 00:29:01.442
Woodsboro murders, with a teenager blowing past him at an alarming speed.

00:29:01.506 --> 00:29:05.034
It's also the anniversary of the day he lost his sister, which means kids

00:29:05.072 --> 00:29:07.654
have decorated the town square with Ghostface paraphernalia.

00:29:07.702 --> 00:29:11.082
He shows up to find his deputy, Judy Hicks, already at work removing them.

00:29:11.136 --> 00:29:14.566
She's harboring a not so secret crush on Sheriff Riley, but he's staying

00:29:14.598 --> 00:29:17.646
faithful to Gale, and if he didn't go for Jennifer Jolie when he was

00:29:17.668 --> 00:29:20.398
single, he's probably not straying from Gale at this point.

00:29:20.484 --> 00:29:23.678
They get a call on the radio about two teenage girls who were stabbed the

00:29:23.684 --> 00:29:25.610
night before and quickly go to investigate.

00:29:25.690 --> 00:29:28.814
Deputy Hicks traces a phone call from the scene of the crime to a bookstore,

00:29:28.862 --> 00:29:32.146
which just happens to be where Sidney Prescott is doing a signing for her

00:29:32.168 --> 00:29:34.211
new publication, Out of Darkness.

00:29:34.211 --> 00:29:36.126
Dewey discovers evidence from the previous night's crime

00:29:36.158 --> 00:29:37.570
planted in Sidney's rental car.

00:29:37.640 --> 00:29:39.410
Guess she's not getting that deposit back.

00:29:39.480 --> 00:29:42.466
Although he doesn't really suspect her, he takes Sid back to the precinct

00:29:42.498 --> 00:29:43.794
for mandatory questioning.

00:29:43.842 --> 00:29:47.106
And to add to the drama, he has to break up an argument between his jealous

00:29:47.138 --> 00:29:48.562
wife and Deputy Hicks.

00:29:48.626 --> 00:29:51.842
Gale blows up on him because she expects to be part of the investigation,

00:29:51.906 --> 00:29:52.890
just like in the past.

00:29:52.960 --> 00:29:56.246
But now that Dewey is sheriff, he's technically not supposed to divulge

00:29:56.278 --> 00:29:59.338
police information to a reporter, and he's forced to send her off.

00:29:59.424 --> 00:30:01.062
This is a major moment for Dewey.

00:30:01.126 --> 00:30:04.118
Perhaps the biggest mistake he made in the first investigation was letting

00:30:04.134 --> 00:30:06.042
Gale distract him while he was on duty.

00:30:06.106 --> 00:30:08.846
Even if they are better off as a team, he's showing that he takes his

00:30:08.868 --> 00:30:10.698
newfound responsibility seriously.

00:30:10.794 --> 00:30:13.854
When Gale declares that she's going rogue, the expression of hurt on his

00:30:13.892 --> 00:30:14.702
face says it all.

00:30:14.756 --> 00:30:17.778
He's risking what's left of his relationship by sticking to the law.

00:30:17.864 --> 00:30:20.814
Eventually, he's going to have to choose between being the perfect sheriff

00:30:20.862 --> 00:30:22.286
or being the perfect husband.

00:30:22.398 --> 00:30:25.554
For now, he places 24 hours police surveillance on Sidney for her protection.

00:30:25.592 --> 00:30:28.482
But that doesn't stop the new Ghostface from taking another

00:30:28.536 --> 00:30:29.810
teenage victim nearby.

00:30:29.890 --> 00:30:33.334
So Sheriff Riley finds himself in the unenviable position of telling his

00:30:33.372 --> 00:30:37.334
community it's going to be fine, when he very much knows it may not be.

00:30:37.372 --> 00:30:40.966
As the killer would immediately demonstrate when Sidney's literary publicist is

00:30:40.988 --> 00:30:43.718
thrown off a parking garage in the middle of his press conference.

00:30:43.814 --> 00:30:46.886
Although being sheriff in the midst of a Scream movie is basically a lose

00:30:46.918 --> 00:30:50.310
lose situation, it's cool to see Dewey in action, calling the shots.

00:30:50.390 --> 00:30:53.878
He's come a long way from the 25 year old taking orders and doing grunt work.

00:30:53.894 --> 00:30:57.102
However, his position requires him to conduct himself in a certain

00:30:57.156 --> 00:31:00.602
manner, as opposed to Gale, who can use less orthodox methods.

00:31:00.666 --> 00:31:04.138
Dewey later receives a call from her as she's staking out the Stabathon Film Fest,

00:31:04.154 --> 00:31:07.502
a gathering of high school film buffs to celebrate the Stab franchise,

00:31:07.566 --> 00:31:09.550
and she thinks the killer is about to strike.

00:31:09.630 --> 00:31:13.294
He mocks her from needing his help after going rogue, causing her to pout

00:31:13.342 --> 00:31:13.954
and hang up.

00:31:13.992 --> 00:31:17.506
He immediately realizes the danger she's in and rushes to her location, only

00:31:17.528 --> 00:31:20.994
to find her car, where he spots Ghostface sneaking up on her on the monitor.

00:31:21.042 --> 00:31:24.646
Unable to do anything about it, he rushes into the barn where Stabathon is

00:31:24.668 --> 00:31:28.054
being held and fires a shot in the mass killer's direction, but not before

00:31:28.092 --> 00:31:31.766
Ghostface takes the name of the event literally and stabs Gale in the shoulder.

00:31:31.788 --> 00:31:34.934
Dewey's concern for his wife trumps his need to catch the killer,

00:31:34.982 --> 00:31:38.678
so he attends to her as Ghostface gets away, jogging next to Gale as she's

00:31:38.694 --> 00:31:41.074
wheeled to an ambulance, Dewey has an epiphany!

00:31:41.074 --> 00:31:43.146
Perhaps thinking over the two times Gale had to do

00:31:43.168 --> 00:31:46.798
the same for him, that is, watching him go away on a stretcher, Dewey makes a pledge.

00:31:46.804 --> 00:31:49.134
- [DEWEY] No more on your own.

00:31:49.332 --> 00:31:51.034
- [DEWEY] It's you and me forever.

00:31:51.162 --> 00:31:52.990
Not a promise he could keep. Anyway.

00:31:53.060 --> 00:31:55.230
Deputy Hicks calls with more grim news.

00:31:55.300 --> 00:31:58.878
Sidney's aunt, Kate Roberts, has lost her life along with two of Dewey's

00:31:58.894 --> 00:32:00.478
officers, Haas and Perkins.

00:32:00.574 --> 00:32:03.826
Without hesitation, Sheriff Riley hits the lights, cues the siren, and

00:32:03.848 --> 00:32:05.326
speeds off to meet Judy at

00:32:05.358 --> 00:32:08.658
Mrs. Roberts, which is not the right spot, as he finds out when he gets a

00:32:08.664 --> 00:32:11.698
panicked phone call from Sidney, who explains that she's at Kirby Reed's

00:32:11.714 --> 00:32:13.490
house and the killer is in the vicinity.

00:32:13.570 --> 00:32:15.542
Notice how Sidney doesn't call 911.

00:32:15.596 --> 00:32:17.042
She just calls Dewey directly.

00:32:17.106 --> 00:32:19.526
I hope to have that level of notoriety one day.

00:32:19.628 --> 00:32:20.838
I mean, I do.

00:32:20.924 --> 00:32:21.372
I do.

00:32:21.372 --> 00:32:21.872
Right now.

00:32:21.900 --> 00:32:22.762
Don't !#$@! with me.

00:32:22.816 --> 00:32:26.326
Dewey orders Deputy Judy to send all units to three two nine Whispering Lane.

00:32:26.358 --> 00:32:30.206
Dewey is no longer the lone cowboy he once was, but this new pair of

00:32:30.228 --> 00:32:33.278
killers are a different breed than Billy Loomis and Stu Macher were, and the

00:32:33.284 --> 00:32:37.360
brigade of officers could not possibly contend with what they would find.

00:32:37.723 --> 00:32:40.795
(IMPACT)

00:32:42.896 --> 00:32:46.530
♪ Ominous Music ♪

00:32:46.530 --> 00:32:50.350
Dewey and the police arrive, only to find out that they were too late.

00:32:50.430 --> 00:32:53.586
When they get to Kirby's house, they find nothing but a living room full of victims.

00:32:53.608 --> 00:32:55.314
Or so it seems.

00:32:55.432 --> 00:32:58.750
The survivors, Jill, Sidney, and Kirby, are transferred to the hospital.

00:32:58.830 --> 00:33:02.146
The only one who is conscious is Jill, and she has an oddly unenthusiastic

00:33:02.178 --> 00:33:04.498
reaction to learning that Sidney was still alive.

00:33:04.594 --> 00:33:08.246
This doesn't showcase Dewey's ineptitude as much as it highlights how he and

00:33:08.268 --> 00:33:11.846
Gale really do work better together than apart, which is proven shortly after.

00:33:11.878 --> 00:33:13.914
When Dewey stops by her room.

00:33:14.032 --> 00:33:15.674
- [DEWEY] She asked if you were okay. 

00:33:15.872 --> 00:33:20.406
- [DEWEY] She thinks you guys should write a book together with your matching wounds.

00:33:20.598 --> 00:33:24.806
- [GALE] Why she was stabbed in the shoulder. How did she know I was, too?

00:33:24.806 --> 00:33:26.478
Dewey and Gale realize it at the same time.

00:33:26.564 --> 00:33:30.106
Jill would not know where Gale's stab wound was unless she was in league

00:33:30.138 --> 00:33:31.502
with the one who created it.

00:33:31.556 --> 00:33:34.478
He rushes back to Sidney's room, where he's greeted with a bedpan to the

00:33:34.484 --> 00:33:38.018
face and beaten down until he's out cold like his first two goarounds with

00:33:38.024 --> 00:33:40.770
Ghostface, he stays down for the entire finale.

00:33:41.430 --> 00:33:43.938
What hit me? Don't ask.

00:33:44.104 --> 00:33:47.726
But for the fourth time now, the trio, this time accompanied by Deputy Hicks,

00:33:47.758 --> 00:33:50.522
are able to take down their deranged adversaries.

00:33:50.606 --> 00:33:53.798
He may not have realized it at the time, but this was the tail end of the

00:33:53.804 --> 00:33:55.394
golden era of Dewey Riley.

00:33:55.442 --> 00:33:59.046
He has Gale, Sidney is safe, and he has a competent deputy working for him

00:33:59.068 --> 00:33:59.650
in Hicks.

00:33:59.730 --> 00:34:02.794
He and Gale recommitted to each other, but at some point over the next

00:34:02.832 --> 00:34:06.666
decade, Gale's claustrophobia pertaining to small town America creeped up

00:34:06.688 --> 00:34:08.666
and threatened their relationship once more.

00:34:08.768 --> 00:34:12.006
This time it was Dewey who had to make concessions, and he left his hometown

00:34:12.038 --> 00:34:14.758
behind to move to New York City, where Gale would become the host of Good

00:34:14.784 --> 00:34:18.606
Morning with Gale Weathers for all of about two months before giving up on

00:34:18.628 --> 00:34:20.602
the marriage to return to Woodsboro.

00:34:20.666 --> 00:34:23.294
For someone who's supposed to be the bravest character in the franchise, he

00:34:23.332 --> 00:34:25.354
doesn't do too well outside of his comfort zone.

00:34:25.402 --> 00:34:29.346
Whereas Gale lasted more than twelve years outside of hers, his old job was

00:34:29.368 --> 00:34:32.658
waiting for him, probably held in the interim by Deputy Judy Hicks, as you

00:34:32.664 --> 00:34:35.454
would expect for the man who is basically a Woodsboro folk hero.

00:34:35.502 --> 00:34:39.054
But the split from Gale seems to just break him with his growing disconnect

00:34:39.102 --> 00:34:41.158
from the people he crafted his identity around.

00:34:41.244 --> 00:34:44.882
He becomes a hermit and moves into a dingy trailer in the outskirts of town.

00:34:44.946 --> 00:34:47.938
I guess he was used to the trailer life from his time on Jennifer Jolie's

00:34:47.954 --> 00:34:50.966
driveway, but it's still a downgrade from the big house he once shared with Gale.

00:34:50.988 --> 00:34:54.346
Dewey has a habit of revisiting the worst moments of his life, and

00:34:54.368 --> 00:34:55.498
he's had quite a few.

00:34:55.584 --> 00:34:59.178
He also becomes an alcoholic, and it seems that his personal issues began to

00:34:59.184 --> 00:35:02.438
affect his work, and eventually he was asked to resign from the Woodsboro

00:35:02.454 --> 00:35:05.434
Police Department and Deputy Hicks was promoted to sheriff.

00:35:05.482 --> 00:35:09.022
Hicks after spending his whole life trying to earn respect, they finally

00:35:09.076 --> 00:35:11.358
stripped the last accolade he had to his name.

00:35:11.444 --> 00:35:13.242
Life became pretty sad for Dewey.

00:35:13.306 --> 00:35:16.334
With his sister's ashes on his mantle, the only thing he had to look forward

00:35:16.372 --> 00:35:18.958
to every day was seeing his ex wife's show on TV.

00:35:19.054 --> 00:35:22.626
With no Ghostface and no one he cared about to protect, Dewey felt that he

00:35:22.648 --> 00:35:23.758
had lost his purpose.

00:35:23.854 --> 00:35:28.626
He continued to sink deeper until 2021, 25 years since Billy Loomis and

00:35:28.648 --> 00:35:32.566
Stu Macher first asked what's your favorite scary movie? Opportunity would

00:35:32.588 --> 00:35:34.258
come knocking at his door.

00:35:34.354 --> 00:35:38.162
Samantha Carpenter and her boyfriend, and definitely not Ghostface Ritchie,

00:35:38.226 --> 00:35:41.506
come around looking for an expert in regards to a new set of Ghostface attacks.

00:35:41.538 --> 00:35:44.470
Experts don't typically fare well in scream.

00:35:44.550 --> 00:35:47.030
Just ask Randy, Meeks, Charlie, and Robbie.

00:35:47.110 --> 00:35:50.058
The fact that they want to talk to him so badly, even when he doesn't want

00:35:50.064 --> 00:35:53.306
to get involved, illustrates that because of his experiences, he still has

00:35:53.328 --> 00:35:56.318
the respect of the younger generation who desperately need his help.

00:35:56.404 --> 00:35:59.098
This is a small win for Dewey, but he's still skeptical.

00:35:59.194 --> 00:36:01.214
-[DEWEY] Give me one good reason why I should talk to you.

