Sidney is a survivor, and there was something noble about it for Dewey.

00:48:02.546 --> 00:48:05.074
He was there to protect Sidney and the people of Woodsboro.

00:48:05.122 --> 00:48:08.066
There was a scene between Dewey and Gale and there was a take they didn't

00:48:08.098 --> 00:48:09.762
use where I was super emotional.

00:48:09.826 --> 00:48:11.842
I sort of adlibbed, I'm a failure.

00:48:11.906 --> 00:48:13.074
I couldn't save Judy.

00:48:13.122 --> 00:48:14.310
I couldn't save my sister.

00:48:14.390 --> 00:48:15.974
I think it was actually too emotional.

00:48:16.022 --> 00:48:17.098
Like, it was too much.

00:48:17.184 --> 00:48:20.118
And a lot of that emotion that I was going through at that time was mourning

00:48:20.134 --> 00:48:20.634
a loss.

00:48:20.710 --> 00:48:23.894
The loss of Wes was heavy on our hearts, especially in that scene.

00:48:23.942 --> 00:48:27.294
The only reason Dewey even made it long enough to become the hero be

00:48:27.332 --> 00:48:30.618
respected by the fandom and become an authority within the franchise is due

00:48:30.634 --> 00:48:33.786
to David Arquette's own drive to be better and earn respect.

00:48:33.898 --> 00:48:37.474
I'm sure the OG 90s fandom will probably never stop imagining different

00:48:37.512 --> 00:48:40.254
scenarios that bring Dewey back as they have for Randy.

00:48:40.302 --> 00:48:44.674
But no matter how you slice it, pun intended, Dewey was meant to die in

00:48:44.712 --> 00:48:45.810
Scream 2022.

00:48:45.880 --> 00:48:50.018
Against all odds and maybe sense, he became the Clint Eastwood of Scream.

00:48:50.114 --> 00:48:54.274
The town hero riding out on his bronco to rid the west of Ghostface.

00:48:54.402 --> 00:48:57.926
If you want more information on the meta insanity that is Scream, click on

00:48:57.948 --> 00:49:01.378
that playlist on the left for my analysis of characters like Randy, Billy

00:49:01.394 --> 00:49:03.254
Loomis, Casey Becker, and others.

00:49:03.372 --> 00:49:07.046
Remember to subscribe to CZ's World for new horrors every week, unless it

00:49:07.068 --> 00:49:08.390
gets held up in review again.

00:49:08.460 --> 00:49:12.110
Ring the death bell for all notification, and I'll see you in the next one,

00:49:12.180 --> 00:49:14.190
assuming we both survive.

